Implemented Vercel Speed Insights for the Next.js project

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights by following the latest official documentation from Vercel's quickstart guide.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Added `@vercel/speed-insights` version 2.0.0 as a project dependency
- Updated package.json to include the new dependency
- Updated pnpm-lock.yaml with all required dependencies

### 2. Component Integration
Modified: `/src/app/layout.tsx`
- Imported `SpeedInsights` component from `@vercel/speed-insights/next`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component at the end of the body tag (after Providers)
- Follows Next.js App Router (v13.5+) best practices as per Vercel documentation

## Implementation Details

The implementation follows the official Vercel Speed Insights quickstart guide:
1. Installed package using pnpm (the project's package manager)
2. Added the SpeedInsights component to the root layout file
3. Positioned the component correctly within the body tag for optimal performance tracking

## Framework Details
- Project: Next.js 16.2.6 with App Router
- Package Manager: pnpm
- TypeScript: Enabled

